<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/37801AKCRRQNMLVLKQJBSQBHRPCKVJJNK>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (Royal Ballet in Cinema)";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/4bebe6a7-2b38-4a93-be4c-b35f62d275e2.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Alice's Adventures in Wonderland</h1><h2>Royal Ballet in Cinema</h2><span><br/></span>Tumble down the rabbit hole in this screening of the ballet adaptation of Lewis Carroll’s famous family story <span class=\"ItalicText\">Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Synopsis</span>:<span><br/></span>At a garden party on a sunny afternoon, Alice is surprised to see her parents’ friend Lewis Carroll transform into a white rabbit. When she follows him down a rabbit hole, events become curiouser and curiouser… As Alice journeys through Wonderland, she encounters countless strange creatures. She’s swept off her feet by the charming Knave of Hearts, who’s on the run for stealing the tarts. Confusion piles upon confusion. Then Alice wakes with a start. Was it all a daydream?<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Christopher Wheeldon’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland</span> burst onto the stage in 2011 in an explosion of colour, stage magic and inventive, sophisticated choreography. Joby Talbot’s score combines contemporary soundworlds with sweeping melodies that gesture to ballet scores of the 19th century. Bob Crowley’s wildly imaginative, eye-popping designs draw on everything from puppetry to projections to make Wonderland wonderfully real. The result shows The Royal Ballet at its best, bringing together world-class dance with enchanting family entertainment and ingenious music and design.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Be prepared for some of the most flamboyant and familiar characters in dance to come face to face, as hip-hop meets ballet in an explosion of colour, choreography and extravagant design.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">* Please note that this is not a live ballet performance – this is a screening of a performance that was filmed.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Kq8zqhqjUIo?si=OyJYY9UUZxpp0XTF/\">Watch the Trailer!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, April 3rd at 7:00 pm<span><br/></span>Sunday, April 4th at 2:00 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2 hours and 50 minutes, plus two intermissions</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span>Adults -<span class=\"BoldText\">$23.00</span> ($17.54+ tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span>Youth (under 20) -<span class=\"BoldText\">$11.50</span>  ($7.45 + tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span>$10 Community Tickets use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Genre: Filmed Ballet, Fantasy, Adventure<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Admission includes complimentary popcorn.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission<span><br/></span>Doors open 45 mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-04-03T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/4bebe6a7-2b38-4a93-be4c-b35f62d275e2.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/location/601APNNMRMBJQQPBSCNQGQHGKKCRPSSGN>;
