<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/31401ACGSQBSNGJMMSMSJDBKPVTCCSKMC>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "By-FOLK-le: A Community Variety Show";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/b47adffd-0177-4425-b990-df3fb6ad2944.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>By-FOLK-le!</h1><span><br/></span>Chester’s beloved community talent show, the <span class=\"BoldText\"><span class=\"ItalicText\">By-FOLK-le is BACK</span></span>!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Join your friends and neighbours, as they take the stage in a celebration of community talent! Songs, monologues, jokes, and surprises abound in this sometimes silly, sometimes stunning, always delightful evening of pre-holiday fun. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Featuring performances by <span class=\"BoldText\">Dark & Stormy</span>, and a bill of all-local talent including: <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Kyle O’Brien</span> - Singer/Songwriter<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Zakary Miller</span> - Oldtimey Canadiana Swing with added Kazoo!<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Sage</span> - Harmonious Singers<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Erin Gore & Andrew Hamson</span> - Poetry with a twist<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Katie Feltmate</span> - Singer/Songwriter<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Kristina Nicoll</span> - Poetry<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Hodgepodge</span> - Teen Vocal Group<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Pots and Pans</span> - Music Duo<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Anavi Davis</span> - World Champion Whistler<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>.... you won’t want to miss this chance to sing, dance, and celebrate the talent that lives in this wonderful community and beyond.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Hosting the show is improv comedy duo <span class=\"BoldText\">Colin and Joe</span>! Colin Dunphy and Joe Harfhouche are regulars around the Halifax comedy scene, and had a stellar show at the 2025 Halifax Fringe Festival. We’re so excited to have them bringing the laughs (and even some games) to By-FOLK-le!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We hope you’ll join us for an evening of wonderful surprises, as Chester takes the stage of its Playhouse! <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, December 12th at 7:30 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2x45 minute sets, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Pay What You Can</span> - suggested $25<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-12-12T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/b47adffd-0177-4425-b990-df3fb6ad2944.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/location/601APNNMRMBJQQPBSCNQGQHGKKCRPSSGN>;
