<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/38201AHNBNPJGLCLVNBPRCDPTCCSQSKKV>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Hay Fever - National Theatre Live";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/96dc1220-f439-48b7-950a-fb7c21467aea.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Hay Fever</h1><h2>National Theatre Live (Filmed Theatre)</h2><span><br/></span>National Theatre Live on screen returns as Emmy and Tony winner Christine Baranski joins Academy Award-nominated stage and screen legend Richard E. Grant in Noël Coward’s irresistible comedy <span class=\"ItalicText\">Hay Fever</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Synopsis</span>:<span><br/></span>Judith Bliss retired from her life-on-stage and she misses the applause. Idling away at their country home, the rest of the family are too self-involved to be a good audience. So, Judith invites a young fan as her guest for the weekend. But unbeknownst to her, each of the Blisses has a guest of their own arriving at the very same time.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Filmed live from the West End, Emily Burns directs this stinging new production. From Wessex Grove and Gavin Kalin Productions.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">A riotous new production</span>” -Metro<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">* Please note that this is a screening of a filmed National Theatre production.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Sunday, May 2 at 2:00 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2 hours and 10 minutes, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span>Adults -<span class=\"BoldText\">$23.00</span> ($17.54+ tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span>Youth (4-19) -<span class=\"BoldText\">$11.50</span>  ($7.45 + tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span>$10 Community Tickets use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Genre: Comedy (Filmed Theatre)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Admission includes complimentary popcorn.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission<span><br/></span>Doors open 45 mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
