<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/35801AHSQHGLDRQDGJQNMNBKJMSLGBGCB>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Ô-Celli Goes to the Movies";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/08b3a087-54bc-4ba4-aa98-1d68c6390250.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Ô-Celli Goes to the Movies</h1><span><br/></span>Our 2027 season begins with <span class=\"BoldText\">Ô-Celli Goes to the Movies</span>, featuring the extraordinary union of eight cellos bringing to life classic movie music, mixed with some of their original arrangements.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Since 2011, the year of their first concerts, Ô-Celli (aka the Eight from Brussels) have embraced a single guiding principle: pleasure! The pleasure they share on the road and on stages across Europe and Canada, the pleasure they see reflected in the audience’s eyes, and the pleasure of continuing to create new projects. Nearly 15 years later, with four albums recorded and dozens of original arrangements to their name, it is still friendship and a passion for their instrument that drive them forward.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>In this new program, the magic shines brighter than ever as they perform the arrangements that marked their early years, alongside iconic themes from films such as <span class=\"ItalicText\">La Strada</span>, <span class=\"ItalicText\">E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial</span>, and <span class=\"ItalicText\">Harry Potter</span>, to name just a few.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Join us for Ô-Celli Goes to the Movies, an evening promising to leave audiences spellbound long after the final note has faded.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HT2Wh3b1aWg&amp;list=PLvePi35JP1xzC9mYc4QjaV_qyVlTOxwmW&amp;index=2/\">Discover &#212;-Celli!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Sunday, January 31st at 2:00 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2x45 minute sets, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$40.00</span>  ($32.46 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$20.00 </span> ($14.92 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$10 Community Tickets</span> use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span>
""";
