<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/37001ARJRQBSGKJPNKCLJJTNSVJDCDBHT>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Oktopus: Brahms, Balkans, & Bagels";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/5dd84410-77e5-4165-8619-0a0868f655f8.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Oktopus</h1><h2>Brahms, Balkans, & Bagels</h2><span><br/></span>Oktopus brings us <span class=\"ItalicText\">Brahms, Balkans, & Bagels</span>, a small marvel of fusion, blending various classical sources, klezmer, a touch of jazz, and—above all—abundant originality and joy.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Brahms, Balkans & Bagels</span> explores how folk traditions have inspired the great classical composers. How did Hungarian folk melodies shake up Franz Liszt? What traces did klezmer leave in Gustav Mahler’s works? How did Zoltán Kodály preserve the rustic flavor of peasant songs in his symphonies? <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>In this colorful concert, classical and folk traditions stand on equal footing, intertwined in touching and virtuosic arrangements. Sometimes festive, sometimes reflective, the music draws tears caught between laughter and emotion, guided by klezmer’s lively dances and ornamentations.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Oktopus stands as a major voice in Canada’s world-music scene, with nearly 350 performances at home and abroad. Hailing from Quebec, whose musical prowess is rooted in klezmer tradition, the octet, dedicated to klezmer music, sets itself apart with a distinctive approach blending classical, Québécois, and jazz influences. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Praised for the quality of their performances and the sophistication of their arrangements, Oktopus has earned numerous national and international awards. Their concerts are passionate and virtuosic, peppered with humor and storytelling. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XadNmHb-pPo/\">Discover Oktopus!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, April 24 at 7:30 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2x45 minute sets, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$35.00</span>  ($28.07 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$17.50</span> ($12.72 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$10 Community Tickets</span> use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-04-24T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/5dd84410-77e5-4165-8619-0a0868f655f8.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/location/601APNNMRMBJQQPBSCNQGQHGKKCRPSSGN>;
