<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/36001AVSBSKQTBCMJCHVTHSQVQCNPBTLJ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The Ella Fitzgerald Tribute with Dee Hernandez";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/89281e40-f69e-4365-ad52-469bdf66e20e.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>The Ella Fitzgerald Tribute</h1><h2>With Dee Hernandez</h2><span><br/></span>Celebrate Valentine’s Day weekend with Atlantic Canada’s own jazz powerhouse, Dee Hernandez, as she brings her acclaimed <span class=\"ItalicText\">Ella Fitzgerald Tribute Tour</span> to the stage for an unforgettable evening of romance, timeless melodies, and heartfelt interpretations of the First Lady of Song’s most beloved classics.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Often referred to as the \"<span class=\"ItalicText\">Queen Of Jazz</span>,\" Ella Fitzgerald rewrote the book of Jazz vocals throughout a storied career that spanned more than 50 years. Her ground-breaking approach gave birth to the style of singing known as \"<span class=\"ItalicText\">scat</span>,\" fearlessly blending tone, rhythm, timing, and improvisation. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>A lifelong admirer of Ella Fitzgerald, Hernandez and her ensemble of accomplished Jazz veterans channel the soul, swing, and spirit of one of her greatest musical idols. Hernandez has also been featured on Saturday Night Jazz and JazzFM, introducing her music to audiences across Canada.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Audiences can expect an evening of timeless standards, from the silky <span class=\"ItalicText\">Misty</span>, to the playful <span class=\"ItalicText\">Mack the Knife</span> and the show stopping <span class=\"ItalicText\">How High the Moon</span>, along with many more classics from the Fitzgerald songbook brought vividly to life.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yRg3xWLlUUQ/\">Discover Dee Hernandez!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, February 13 at 7:30 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2x45 minute sets, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$50.00</span>  ($47.37+ taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$25.00 </span> ($22.37 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$10 Community Tickets</span> use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
